From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: add the cpu-sleep idle state

The H616 has no management processor, so its TF-A port could not offer
any CPU_SUSPEND state and the SoC had no cpuidle driver beyond WFI.
TF-A (patch "feat(allwinner): offer CPU_SUSPEND natively on the H616")
now powers a single core down through the CPUIDLE hardware block, which
powers it back up as soon as the GIC has an interrupt pending for it.

Describe that state so the PSCI cpuidle driver can use it. TF-A amends
the DTB it finds with the same description, but U-Boot does not propagate
that into a separately loaded kernel DTB, hence the static node (TF-A
skips its amendment when /cpus/idle-states exists). The power state ID
follows the TF-A sunxi encoding (4 bits per level, 3 = off at the CPU
level, power-down type). The core's architected timer stops, the sun4i
timer at 0x03009000 serves as broadcast clock event device.

Latencies are initial estimates for the TF-A round trip and the residency
is conservative (the vendor firmware advertises 46/59/3570 us); they are
to be refined with measurements.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 			device_type = "cpu";
 			reg = <0>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_CPUX>;
 			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			i-cache-size = <0x8000>;
@@ -45,6 +46,7 @@
 			device_type = "cpu";
 			reg = <1>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_CPUX>;
 			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			i-cache-size = <0x8000>;
@@ -61,6 +63,7 @@
 			device_type = "cpu";
 			reg = <2>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_CPUX>;
 			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			i-cache-size = <0x8000>;
@@ -77,6 +80,7 @@
 			device_type = "cpu";
 			reg = <3>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_CPUX>;
 			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			i-cache-size = <0x8000>;
@@ -88,6 +92,19 @@
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache>;
 		};
 
+		idle-states {
+			entry-method = "psci";
+
+			cpu_sleep: cpu-sleep {
+				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00010003>;
+				local-timer-stop;
+				entry-latency-us = <100>;
+				exit-latency-us = <150>;
+				min-residency-us = <4000>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		l2_cache: l2-cache {
 			compatible = "cache";
 			cache-level = <2>;
-- 
